Start a dev server by name from .claude/launch.json. If .claude/launch.json doesn't exist, create it first with this format:
{
  "version": "0.0.1",
  "configurations": [
    {
      "name": "<unique-name>",
      "runtimeExecutable": "<command>",
      "runtimeArgs": ["<args>"],
      "port": <port>
    }
  ]
}
Set "runtimeExecutable" to the command (e.g. "npm"), "runtimeArgs" to the arguments (e.g. ["run", "dev"]), and "port" to the server port. An optional "url" (http/https) opens the preview there instead of http://localhost:<port>. A localhost "url" must be just the server's origin — no path or query, matching the entry's port — for example "https://localhost:8443" or "http://app.localhost:3000"; to show a specific page, navigate after the preview opens. Non-localhost URLs may carry paths and are subject to the user's permission and the organization's browsing policy. A configuration with "url" and no command attaches to an already-running server. Only include servers you actually need to preview. Reuses the server if already running. ALWAYS use this instead of Bash for running servers. If the deliverable is already published as an Artifact, update the Artifact instead of starting a server to show it.

content.text:
Sol 6.1 terminó la revisión con 13 hallazgos. Ya le mandé a Sonnet esos hallazgos y lo que pediste:

- **2,5 veces más grande:** queda en un solo valor ajustable, `EntityScale`, y todas las medidas lo siguen (altura de vuelo, radio del punto débil, colisión, luces, cámara de la prueba automática). Si algún nivel se queda bajo o pequeño para ella, me lo dirá.
- **Tentáculos menos tiesos:**
  - ondulación más amplia y lenta, distinta en cada tentáculo;
  - las puntas siguen al cuerpo con retraso y se pasan un poco de largo;
  - cuelgan con gravedad aunque el cuerpo se incline;
  - de vez en cuando uno se enrosca.
- **Un poco de luz en los tentáculos:** 3 o 4 luces verdes tenues, más un destello del material al disparar y al recibir golpes. El parámetro de destello del material ya lo añadí yo y subí un poco el brillo del holograma.
- **Mis correcciones:**
  - la luz del ojo pasa a ser un foco hacia delante, para que el caparazón vuelva a verse como metal oscuro;
  - las explosiones, la línea de visión y la altura del pecho pasan a medirse desde el caparazón.
- **Lo más serio de Sol:**
  - la colisión invisible de abajo todavía recibe espadazos y hechizos de suelo;
  - el tentáculo podía quedarse estirado tras un ataque cancelado;
  - al volar puede atravesar techos;
  - a menos de 20 fps se mueve más lento;
  - dos mediciones de la prueba automática podían dar por bueno algo que está mal, y los tests aceptaban implementaciones incorrectas.

Cuando Sonnet termine, verifico compilación, tests y capturas, hago el commit y te aviso para que la pruebes.

input.message:
New owner feedback on the tentacles; it changes item B. The owner watched the last smoke run and said (translated): "the tentacle movements looked erratic and random, not purposeful."

So item B ("livelier tentacles") must NOT add more random noise. Make the motion read as intentional and coordinated, as a creature that swims and hunts:

1. **One shared rhythm, not ten independent wiggles.** Drive all chains from a single body "stroke" cycle, like a jellyfish or octopus pulse:
   - the tentacles gather in, then push out;
   - each chain is offset by a small, ordered phase (around the ring, by its angle around the body), not a random phase;
   - the stroke speeds up when the Entity moves fast or prepares an attack, and slows when it idles.
2. **The motion follows intent:**
   - **when it moves:** the tentacles trail opposite to the velocity and stream behind it;
   - **when it targets the player (aggro):** the front tentacles lift and orient toward the player, and the rear ones stay back;
   - **windup:** all tentacles draw in or coil, and then the chosen one strikes (the reach);
   - **on a hit:** a coordinated recoil, all of them flinching away from the hit direction, then they settle;
   - **on death:** the limp you already have.
3. **Remove or strongly reduce the random elements:** the per-chain random phases and frequencies, and the "occasional random curl". Any curl must be motivated, for example the tentacles nearest the player curling toward it.
4. **Keep the secondary motion:** the per-bone follow-through and the gravity hang make the purposeful motion look physical. Use it to smooth the motion, not as noise.

Smoke: add one line, `SMOKE entity sync=%.2f`. It is the mean correlation of the chains' bend phase with the shared stroke over 1 s, and it must be > 0.6, to prove the motion is coordinated. Also describe in your report how each state looks.

